# Google Jobs markup and Indexing API

Do not ship a public job page that is 200 / indexable / not expired without `JobPosting` JSON-LD. That combination dropped GSC Job Postings Valid in Aug 2026 while web search still saw the URL.

## JobPosting (`buildJobJsonLd`)

- Live + indexable + not expired + ≥80 char real body → emit `JobPosting`. Never return `null` only because location is `"Remote"` with no country.
- Every `TELECOMMUTE` JobPosting must include `applicantLocationRequirements`. GSC treats a missing field as a critical Job Postings error (listings become ineligible).
- Worldwide remote: `jobLocationType: TELECOMMUTE` plus `AdministrativeArea` named `Worldwide`. Do **not** invent `USA` or emit `Worldwide` as a Country.
- `Remote (USA)` / a real country: `Country` in `applicantLocationRequirements`. Regions (Europe, APAC) use `AdministrativeArea`, not a fake Country.
- `Full-time` / `Part-time` / `Contract` / `N/A` in the location column are misfiled **job types**, not places. Map them to `employmentType`, ignore as Place, emit `TELECOMMUTE` + `Worldwide`. Never invent `USA`.
- Onsite/hybrid without a parseable Place: fall back to `TELECOMMUTE` + `Worldwide` rather than omitting JobPosting on a live indexable page.
- Never strip ISO country codes `CA` / `IN` / other alias values as US state abbreviations — that deleted `jobLocation` and dropped JobPosting on Toronto, Bangalore, Canada, etc. (Aug 2026 Valid crash).
- Parse `City, Illinois` (full US state name) and `City, Greece` (country name) into a Place with `addressCountry`.
- `validThrough` = `jobPostingValidThrough()` (newest of `published_at` / `created_at` + 30d). Never `published_at + 30d` alone — source posted dates are often weeks older than ingest.
- `url` must be `siteUrl + jobPublicPath` (`/{company}/{slug}`). Never `/jobs/{uuid}` when the company is routeable.

## Indexing API (`.github/scripts/google-indexing.mjs`)

- Canonical URL = `jobPublicPath`. Never the first 8 chars of `external_id`.
- Client URL env: `NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL || SUPABASE_URL`. Workflows must set **both**.
- Select live public jobs in the 30-day newest-stamp window (not only `created_at` last 7 days). Paginate; do not rely on `.limit(50000)` returning more than 1000.
- After a schema change, bump `SCHEMA_EPOCH` so existing URLs get `URL_UPDATED` again (200/day quota).
- Prefer refreshing URLs already in `google-indexing-state.json` (Google already knows them) before brand-new inventory.
- `URL_DELETED` for state URLs that redirect / expired / lost curated-jd — verify with a targeted lookup, not only the capped live scan. Run removes before publishes.
- `isPublicJobPage` + `isJobExpired` still apply. Do not ping uncurated or thin bodies.

## Sitemap

Job sitemaps use `companyJobsDateOrFilter` (`published_at OR created_at`). Never AND `created_at` with a published_at window — that hides live jobs Google already has.
- Never edge-cache an empty job urlset. Reject empty Cache API hits; bump `SITEMAP_CACHE_EPOCH` after poisoning. Empty builds use `no-store`.
- Do not `select description` on sitemap chunk builds — fat text + OR date filter caused PostgREST timeouts that were swallowed into empty cached urlsets.
- Use `withTimeoutFallback` + split `created_at` / `published_at` complement queries — never hang a Worker on OR + tags.
- Rethrow non-timeout Supabase errors from chunk builds; timeout → return partial urlset (uncached), not an infinite hang.

Tests: `src/lib/google-jobs-invariants.test.ts` + `src/lib/sitemap-cache.test.ts`. Live canary: `.github/scripts/google-jobs-canary.mjs`. Docs: `docs/JOB_PAGE_RULES.md`.
